{"school":{"dbn":"31R049","name":"I.S. 49 Berta A. Dreyfus","boro":"Staten Island","district":"31","district_label":"District 31","report_type":"EMS","report_types":"EMS","school_type":"Middle","grades":"6 to 8","status":"open","enrollment":338,"enrollment_year":"2024-25","address":"101 WARREN STREET, STATEN ISLAND, NY 10304","phone":"718-981-0502","website":"www.sites.google.com/a/berta49.org/berta49/","directory_url":"https://www.myschools.nyc/en/schools/middle-school/63619","accessibility":"Partially Accessible","overview":"Dreyfus Intermediate School 49 is a Title I Community School consisting of\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0083\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u00a0students from grades six through eight. Many of our students and families are faced with adversity, consequently deeming student attendance an issue at Dreyfus Intermediate. We are diligently working to increase family involvement, to build confidence and trust in the work we are doing, and ensure that our students are receiving support through a range of social and emotional partnerships within the community school structure. We have increased our partnerships with community-based organizations to support students and families. Some of these strategic partnerships include the YMCA, Big Brother Big Sister Literacy Program, Seamen's Society for Children, Girl\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0083\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0083\u00c2\u0082\u00c3\u0082\u00c2\u00a0UniverCITY, SUNDOG Theatre, 21st Century Community Learning Centers, Salvation Army, the Jewish Community Center, Urban Advantage, Safe Passages, Liberty Partnership, and the Jewish Board. These community partnerships allow our students to feel safe, supported, and valued during and after the school day, through social-emotional, enrichment and academic support programs.","start_time":"08:15am","end_time":"02:35pm","languages":null,"subway":null,"bus":"S51, S52, S74, S76, S78, S84, S86, SIM30","shared_building":"0","neighborhood"